---
description: General rules for working in this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

- Before implementing, outline the request and the steps you will take, then wait for approval.
- If the request is unclear, ask before changing code.
- Comment only when needed to explain why code is written the way it is.
- Follow existing conventions in this repo.
- Update READMEs and `.cursor/rules/` when a change affects how the project is built, tested, or worked on.
- If an approach fails, revert the dysfunctional change rather than leaving it in place.
- Remove throwaway debug files after you are done.
- Search for current package versions before installing.
- If several solutions are reasonable, ask which one to use.
- Do not present guesses as fact. If unconfirmed, say so and label [Inference], [Speculation], or [Unverified].
